1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:08,000
HAVEN | Product overview • Reservation entry • Invoice entry

2
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:18,000
Start with the dashboard: daily priorities, review queues, and recent activity.

3
00:00:18,000 --> 00:00:28,000
Search across records and jump directly to the bill, property, or reservation you need.

4
00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:33,000
Enter a reservation | Property and dates → reviewed quote → saved stay

5
00:00:33,000 --> 00:00:42,000
Open Reservations, then New booking to enter the property and stay dates.

6
00:00:42,000 --> 00:00:49,000
Select Hale Mālie and enter the arrival date: 9 November 2026.

7
00:00:49,000 --> 00:00:57,000
Enter the departure date: 13 November. This example is a four-night stay.

8
00:00:57,000 --> 00:01:05,000
Hold the nights while you prepare and review the booking quote.

9
00:01:05,000 --> 00:01:12,000
Calculate the booking quote from the property’s published prices.

10
00:01:12,000 --> 00:01:20,000
Add the guest or booking reference so the stay is easy to recognize.

11
00:01:20,000 --> 00:01:30,000
The four nights total $1,000 in rent plus $30 in disclosed fees: $1,030.

12
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:37,000
Accept the reviewed quote and confirm the booking.

13
00:01:37,000 --> 00:01:47,000
HAVEN saves the reservation and its folio together, with the guest reference and stay dates.

14
00:01:47,000 --> 00:01:57,000
Open the folio to see the saved nightly rent and fee lines for this stay.

15
00:01:57,000 --> 00:02:02,000
Enter a property invoice | Source PDF → coded bill → balanced service lines

16
00:02:02,000 --> 00:02:12,000
Begin with the source invoice: vendor, property, service details, dates, and the $185 total.

17
00:02:12,000 --> 00:02:20,000
Open Bills to create the invoice’s working record in Bill Entry Desk.

18
00:02:20,000 --> 00:02:27,000
Choose Create Bill. Start with a new payables draft.

19
00:02:27,000 --> 00:02:36,000
Select the vendor, the Cleaning & linen expense account, and the exact HM-01 property.

20
00:02:36,000 --> 00:02:46,000
Enter the invoice number, bill date, due date, and the $185 source total.

21
00:02:46,000 --> 00:02:47,200
Add a clear description of the property service.

22
00:02:47,200 --> 00:02:48,400
Add a clear description of the property service.

23
00:02:48,400 --> 00:02:54,400
Add a clear description of the property service.

24
00:02:54,400 --> 00:03:02,400
Save the draft. The selected source PDF will stay linked to the bill.

25
00:03:02,400 --> 00:03:11,400
The saved draft keeps the invoice identity, property coding, and source document together.

26
00:03:11,400 --> 00:03:19,400
Save the first allocation: $150 for departure cleaning at Hale Mālie.

27
00:03:19,400 --> 00:03:26,400
Add a second line for the remaining $35 linen service.

28
00:03:26,400 --> 00:03:34,400
Give the linen line its account, property, and description, then save it.

29
00:03:34,400 --> 00:03:44,400
Both saved lines total $185. The allocation strip shows Balanced, with no remaining difference.

30
00:03:44,400 --> 00:03:53,400
Keep the invoice date and service date distinct, with the reviewed period recorded alongside them.

31
00:03:53,400 --> 00:04:01,400
The original source PDF remains attached as the bill’s Primary invoice.

32
00:04:01,400 --> 00:04:11,400
The invoice is saved, coded, balanced, and supported by its source document.

33
00:04:11,400 --> 00:04:19,400
From the stay to its source records | One workspace for reservations, property work, and accounting.
